      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2><details class="ba-faq"><summary>Who should avoid ashwagandha?</summary><p>NCCIH advises that ashwagandha may be unsafe during pregnancy and that people with certain conditions or taking medications should speak to a healthcare provider first.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>What part of the plant is Ashwagandha powder made from?</summary><p>The root of Withania somnifera, milled into a fine, earthy powder.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>How is Ashwagandha traditionally taken?</summary><p>Traditionally in warm milk or ghee, often in the evening as part of a wind-down routine.</p></details>
